## 3. Available Audit Options

| Option | Linux | Windows | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| Standard audit | No additional argument | No additional parameter | Audit PHP builds and compliance |
| Fix-date cutoff | `CUTOFF="YYYY-MM-DD"` | As implemented in the script | Compare builds with the advisory fix date |
| CSV header | `--csv-header` | `-CsvHeader` | Generate reporting column names |
| CSV output | `--csv` | `-Csv` | Output a server-level CSV record |
| List domains | `--list-domains` | `-ListDomains` | Identify domains requiring investigation |

The fix-date cutoff syntax shown above is for Linux. Use only the parameters actually supported by the published Windows script.

