## 4. Understanding Audit Results

| Result | Meaning | Recommended action |
|---|---|---|
| `PATCHED` | Supported PHP build meets the configured patch criteria | No immediate patch action identified by this check |
| `NOT PATCHED (EOL)` | PHP version is unsupported | Migrate websites and plan component removal |
| `NOT PATCHED (old build)` | Installed build predates the required fix | Update the relevant PHP component |
| `NOT PATCHED (unknown build)` | Build date or package information cannot be verified | Investigate and verify the installed package |
| `RESTART NEEDED` | A running process may still use an old PHP binary | Restart the affected service during an approved maintenance window |

Do not treat unknown build information as a successful security check.

